B.bpd=new A.c("When it became clear that astrology as a 'physics of fate' was untenable, its main and cleverest defender took the stage: astropsychology.\n\nIts argument was a masterstroke. It went like this: 'You've all misunderstood! Astrology was never about appearance or events. It's a language for describing the psyche. It's a map of our soul, our innate talents, our psychological complexes, and our points of growth.'\n\nThis elegant maneuver allowed astrology to retreat from the battlefield where it was losing to facts and take refuge in the territory of the subjective, the subtle, and the immeasurable\u2014the depths of human psychology. But is this fortress truly so impregnable?",null,null,B.a,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
