B.bqq=new A.c("The verdict of our investigation is clear: the traditional model, based on the cause-and-effect influence of the planets, is an intellectual dead end. Neither predictive astrology nor its psychological version can withstand a collision with facts and logic. Their foundation crumbles.\n\nIt would seem the case could be closed. But this is where the real mystery begins.\n\nBecause, despite all its logical inconsistency, astrology stubbornly refuses to die. And the reason is simple: anyone who has seriously engaged with it knows that strange, inexplicable feeling. The feeling when a vague description suddenly hits the mark with pinpoint accuracy. When a prediction that shouldn't have come true suddenly proves prophetic.\n\nThis is the central paradox. On one hand, a broken, non-working mechanism of 'influence.' On the other, a persistent, recurring 'signal in the noise'\u2014moments of astonishing accuracy that occur far more often than simple probability theory would allow.\n\nHow is this possible? How can a system with a flawed premise at its core occasionally produce correct results?\n\nIt can only mean one thing: there is a grain of truth in astrology. But it is buried so deep under layers of myths and false interpretations that we have ceased to see it. We are trying to start a car by admiring the design of its body, not realizing that its engine is located somewhere else entirely and runs on a different kind of fuel.",null,null,B.a,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
